<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">No Motherland Without You</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 당신이 없으면 조국도 없다, Dangsini eopseumyeon jogukdo eopda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;No Motherland Without You&quot;, also called &quot;Ode to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-jong-il">Kim Jong Il</a>&quot;, is a North Korean song about the country's second supreme leader, Kim Jong Il. It was first released in 1993, with music by Hwang Jin-yong and words by Ri Jong-o. Written especially for Kim Jong Il, it is regarded as his signature song, and it extols his proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talent">talents</a> and virtues and the people's loyalty to him.</p></div>
